	'wk_offices_h' => 'How do we run dining services in office environments?',
	'wk_offices_b' => 'In corporate offices like Alder & Reeve Accountants, where we serve 120 lunches daily, the lunchroom provides a quiet midday pause for administrative and professional teams. Office dining rooms typically operate with compact commercial pantries or open kitchen passes, accommodating concentrated lunch traffic between 11:30 and 13:30. What changes in office settings is the focus on rapid counter service, quiet kitchen equipment, and light, nutritious midday menus that support afternoon focus. With three dedicated team members adhering to our one-to-forty staffing ratio, service remains swift and dining spaces stay organized throughout the lunch break.',
	'wk_factories_h' => 'How are factory canteens structured for multi-shift production?',
	'wk_factories_b' => 'Manufacturing sites require hearty, high-protein set lunches and flexible schedules to accommodate rigorous physical work. At Northgate Components, where our team prepares 420 lunches daily, service operates across two distinct production shifts. Factory canteens require larger dining halls, robust tray slides, and rapid replenishment so workers can maximize their break time without waiting in long queues. What changes here is the addition of a secondary shift service window at $1.10 per lunch, coordinated closely with production supervisors to ensure workers on both shifts receive identical meal variety and fresh temperature-controlled food.',
	'wk_campuses_h' => 'How do campus dining halls support students and faculty?',
	'wk_campuses_b' => 'Educational institutions demand versatile dining layouts capable of handling large waves of diners arriving between lectures. At Fernhill Technical College, our on-site team serves 310 lunches each weekday to students, faculty, and administrative staff. What changes on campuses is the dining floor scale and the necessity for multiple queueing points to prevent congestion. With eight dedicated staff members on the floor and behind the pass, students and faculty enjoy balanced set meals featuring two main choices and a plant-based alternative, served efficiently within narrow class transition windows.',
	'wk_depots_h' => 'How do depot break rooms accommodate transport logistics crews?',
	'wk_depots_b' => 'Logistics and distribution hubs operate around the clock, with drivers and warehouse staff taking staggered breaks around transport schedules. At Bayline Distribution, we serve 180 lunches daily, supporting both daytime logistics crews and overnight drivers. What changes in depot facilities is the need for flexible holding times and specialized night-shift hot boxes priced at $6.80 per box. These insulated meal boxes keep evening meals hot and fresh for transport staff arriving well after standard daytime service hours, ensuring that off-peak logistics teams enjoy the same wholesome food as daytime workers.',
