	'sites_c1_h' => 'Where are Mahora Foods lunchrooms located across our regional districts?',
	'sites_c1_b' => 'Our service network covers thirty-eight workplace dining rooms organized across four operational districts. In Northshore, we manage twelve lunchrooms serving manufacturing and commercial operations. The Harbour district encompasses eleven active facilities located in industrial hubs and academic centers. Central district includes nine corporate lunchrooms serving financial and professional office firms. In Westfields, six operational lunchrooms support transport facilities, logistics depots, and regional businesses. This regional grouping allows head of site operations Wei-Lin Chen and our operations leads to visit kitchens regularly, maintain food safety standards, and provide direct daily support to on-site supervisors.',
	'sites_c2_h' => 'What lunchroom sites operate across our network?',
	'sites_c2_b' => 'Our network includes diverse operational sites that reflect our flexible workplace catering model. In the Northshore district, Northgate Components operates as a manufacturing factory where our team serves 420 lunches daily across two production shifts. In Central district, Alder & Reeve Accountants runs a corporate office lunchroom providing 120 lunches daily. Within the Harbour district, Fernhill Technical College functions as an academic campus where we serve 310 lunches each weekday. In Westfields, Bayline Distribution operates a freight depot where we deliver 180 lunches daily, including insulated hot boxes for overnight logistics personnel.',
	'sites_c3_h' => 'How does daily kitchen management run at a representative site?',
	'sites_c3_b' => 'A close examination of our service at Northgate Components illustrates our operational discipline in a busy facility. Serving 420 lunches daily across two distinct factory shifts requires eleven dedicated kitchen staff members working in synchronized coordination. The team initiates vegetable chopping and sauce preparation at 06:30, readying hot holding units for the first lunch service window. Pass lines are replenished continuously so workers entering the canteen during shift changeovers receive hot meals immediately. Site supervisors oversee tray returns, dish sanitizing, and hygiene documentation, ensuring the canteen remains orderly and ready for subsequent production breaks.',
