	'case-studies_tab' => 'Case studies',
	'case-studies_c1_h' => 'Northgate Components: Managing two-shift dining for 420 factory workers',
	'case-studies_c1_b' => 'At Northgate Components, a manufacturing plant with 420 employees, the operational challenge centered on concentrated thirty-minute lunch breaks across two distinct shifts. Long lines previously delayed workers and left second-shift crews with depleted food selections. Mahora Foods introduced an eleven-person kitchen crew adhering strictly to our 1:40 staffing ratio, along with a dual-station pass system. Morning prep begins at 06:30, with dishes portioned for the primary 11:30 shift and fresh replenishment cooked specifically for the second shift. Meals are served at the contract rate of $7.60 per lunch plus the standard $1.10 second-shift supplement.',
	'case-studies_c2_h' => 'Alder & Reeve Accountants: Providing daily meals for 120 office staff',
	'case-studies_c2_b' => 'Alder & Reeve Accountants required a dependable lunch service for 120 office employees within a facility that had a compact preparation area and no dedicated extraction hoods. Staff members frequently left the building for food, causing fragmented break times. Mahora Foods established a three-person on-site team that prepares roasted mains and fresh sides using high-efficiency commercial equipment suitable for office buildings. Operating within the standard $8.40 per lunch tier, our cooks finish plating by 11:15, allowing employees to enjoy hot, balanced lunches on-site between 11:30 and 13:30 in a calm and orderly environment.',
	'case-studies_c3_h' => 'Fernhill Technical College: Streamlining campus dining for 310 diners',
	'case-studies_c3_b' => 'Fernhill Technical College faced severe canteen congestion, serving 310 students and faculty members during compressed forty-five-minute break intervals between lectures. Slow food delivery often resulted in diners missing meal opportunities entirely. Mahora Foods reconfigured the service line into two parallel hot passes and assigned eight kitchen staff members to oversee food preparation and counter distribution. By introducing our structured four-week cycle featuring two hot mains and one plant-based option at $7.60 per lunch, both hot passes now serve the whole campus within the midday service window.',
	'case-studies_c4_h' => 'Bayline Distribution: Delivering 180 day and night meals for depot staff',
	'case-studies_c4_b' => 'Bayline Distribution operates a busy transport depot where 180 logistics personnel and drivers work irregular schedules, including overnight freight shifts. The primary difficulty was providing hot, nutritious meals to nighttime drivers who arrived long after the lunchroom closed. Mahora Foods introduced daytime kitchen service at $8.40 per lunch alongside dedicated night-shift hot boxes priced at $6.80 per box. Daytime cooks prepare and seal these insulated hot boxes during afternoon wrap-up, placing them in temperature-controlled holding cabinets for night-shift workers. Five on-site staff maintain the facility and coordinate daytime counter service.',
